class ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_mapper {
    {static} +to_entity(entry : messaging::telemetry_log_entry, tenant_id : string) : telemetry_entity
    {static} +to_domain(entity : telemetry_entity) : messaging::telemetry_log_entry
    {static} +to_domain(entity : telemetry_stats_hourly_entity) : domain::telemetry_stats
    {static} +to_domain(entity : telemetry_stats_daily_entity) : domain::telemetry_stats
    {static} +to_entity(sample : messaging::nats_server_sample, tenant_id : string) : nats_server_sample_entity
    {static} +to_domain(entity : nats_server_sample_entity) : messaging::nats_server_sample
    {static} +to_entity(sample : messaging::nats_stream_sample, tenant_id : string) : nats_stream_sample_entity
    {static} +to_domain(entity : nats_stream_sample_entity) : messaging::nats_stream_sample
    {static} +to_entity(sample : messaging::service_sample) : service_sample_entity
    {static} +to_domain(entity : service_sample_entity) : messaging::service_sample
}
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_mapper"
Stateless: every method is static, and each pair converts one
protocol payload to its entity and back. The log and NATS
converters take the tenant id; the service converter does not,
because a service heartbeat is not tenant-scoped.
end note

class ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_repository {
    +sql() : string
    +create(ctx : context, entry : messaging::telemetry_log_entry) : void
    +create_batch(ctx : context, batch : domain::telemetry_batch) : size_t
    +query(ctx : context, q : messaging::telemetry_query) : vector<messaging::telemetry_log_entry>
    +count(ctx : context, q : messaging::telemetry_query) : uint64_t
    +read_by_session(ctx : context, session_id : uuid, limit : uint32_t) : vector<messaging::telemetry_log_entry>
    +read_by_account(ctx : context, account_id : uuid, start : time_point, end : time_point, limit : uint32_t) : vector<messaging::telemetry_log_entry>
    +read_hourly_stats(ctx : context, q : domain::telemetry_stats_query) : vector<domain::telemetry_stats>
    +read_daily_stats(ctx : context, q : domain::telemetry_stats_query) : vector<domain::telemetry_stats>
    +get_summary(ctx : context, hours : uint32_t) : domain::telemetry_summary
    +count_errors(ctx : context, source_name : string, hours : uint32_t) : uint64_t
    +delete_old_logs(ctx : context, older_than : time_point) : uint64_t
    +insert_server_sample(ctx : context, sample : messaging::nats_server_sample) : void
    +insert_stream_samples(ctx : context, samples : vector<messaging::nats_stream_sample>) : void
    +query_server_samples(ctx : context, q : messaging::nats_server_samples_query) : vector<messaging::nats_server_sample>
    +query_stream_samples(ctx : context, q : messaging::nats_stream_samples_query) : vector<messaging::nats_stream_sample>
    +insert_service_sample(ctx : context, sample : messaging::service_sample) : void
    +list_service_samples(ctx : context) : vector<messaging::service_sample>
}
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_repository"
The component's only database writer and reader. Every method
takes a database context and runs under a skip_telemetry_guard,
so the repository's own logging does not re-enter the sink. The
sample methods are what the two NATS sample handlers and the
heartbeat handler call; the log methods serve the logs subject.
end note

class ores::telemetry::database::repository::stream_output <<facet>> {
    {static} +operator<<(os : ostream&, v : telemetry_entity) : ostream&
    {static} +operator<<(os : ostream&, v : telemetry_stats_hourly_entity) : ostream&
    {static} +operator<<(os : ostream&, v : telemetry_stats_daily_entity) : ostream&
}
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::stream_output"
Free functions declared beside the three entities that carry
one. The two sample entities declare no stream operator.
end note

' --- the ORM settings the entity bodies repeat

note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_entity"
ORM settings:
- Schema:    public
- Tablename: ores_telemetry_logs_tbl
TimescaleDB hypertable partitioned by timestamp; the primary
key is (id, timestamp).
end note
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_stats_hourly_entity"
ORM settings:
- Schema:    public
- Tablename: ores_telemetry_stats_hourly_vw
A continuous aggregate view, not a table.
end note
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::telemetry_stats_daily_entity"
ORM settings:
- Schema:    public
- Tablename: ores_telemetry_stats_daily_vw
A continuous aggregate view with the component breakdown.
end note
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::nats_server_sample_entity"
ORM settings:
- Schema:    public
- Tablename: ores_telemetry_nats_server_samples_tbl
Hypertable; the primary key is (sampled_at, tenant_id).
end note
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::nats_stream_sample_entity"
ORM settings:
- Schema:    public
- Tablename: ores_telemetry_nats_stream_samples_tbl
Hypertable; the primary key is (sampled_at, tenant_id,
stream_name).
end note
note right of "ores::telemetry::database::repository::service_sample_entity"
ORM settings:
- Schema:    public
- Tablename: ores_telemetry_service_samples_tbl
Hypertable; the primary key is (sampled_at, service_name,
instance_id), so the table keeps one row per report.
end note

